From 20b530d80a6a5c7f9aea1b931fc0a3814f815489 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:25:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 068/108] gpu: resolve feed for depth (k_24_8) and k_32_FLOAT
 textures, lower texture parts, per-format registry

- Feed pipelines for R32_SFLOAT targets: k_32_FLOAT render targets read
  through their float or bit-exact uint transfer view (resolve_feed_uint.frag),
  and kD24S8 depth render targets into k_24_8 textures (loaded as R32_SFLOAT
  depth, resolve_feed_depth.frag, depth / stencil transfer source set).
- Resolves into the lower part of a tiled 32bpp texture (an address a whole
  number of 32-row bands after its base) feed that texture at that row: the
  shadow map's two 1024x1024 cascades go to one 1024x2048 texture.
- The feed registry is keyed by base and format: the game samples some
  resolved memory both as k_24_8 and as k_8_8_8_8.
- Diagnostics: each distinct feed / reject / depth resolve / depth or float
  texture load is logged once.
- Battle: texture loads 2.5 -> 1.24 ms per frame, GPU work 12.95 -> 12.5-12.6
  Mcycles at 475 MHz; frames look the same.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

